    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d112">

                <pb facs="0258" n="146" xml:id="pg146"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.6111/373: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate Peace to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-18T21:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 18, 1919,
                                9 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 10:07 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>2635. Further referring to your 2294, June 13, 4 p.m.<anchor n="18"
                        xml:id="d112-f1"/> President states:</p>
                <p>“Of course, if Martens is a German subject and can be legitimately deported, I
                    have no objection because such grounds would be abundant, but I hope the
                    evidence is in fact complete.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">American Mission</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
